Organic-history scenario fixtures
=================================

These fixtures are intentionally small, generated-map-compatible scenario
fixtures for automated testing. They are not hand-authored historical maps.

Freeciv scenarios are savegames with a `[scenario]` section and
`is_scenario=TRUE`. The organic-history fixtures use the upstream
`data/scenarios/earth-small.sav` map as the first fixed-geography base because
it is compact (80x50), ruleset-unlocked, map-only (`players=FALSE`), and has
start positions for AI-only tests.

Fixtures:

- `earth_ancient_v0.sav`
- `earth_ancient_v1.sav`
- `earth_medieval_v0.sav`
- `earth_medieval_v1.sav`
- `earth_1450_v0.sav`
- `earth_1450_v1.sav`

The v0 fixtures are infrastructure fixtures with distinct scenario metadata over
the same small Earth base map. The v1 fixtures are generated by
`tools/organic_history/create_scenario_fixture.py --include-v1 --all-v1-plans`;
they start from the same base map, then use the Freeciv server/Lua edit APIs and
`scensave` to create fixed AI actors and starting cities.

The v1 historical actor/start plans are structured data in:

- `data/organic_history/scenarios/earth_ancient_v1_starts.json`
- `data/organic_history/scenarios/earth_medieval_v1_starts.json`
- `data/organic_history/scenarios/earth_1450_v1_starts.json`

Athens and Parsa are slightly offset from their earth-small nation start tiles
so the compact 80x50 map can keep the default city spacing.

The v1 starts plan also carries era setup:

- starting gold
- known era technologies
- current research targets
- diplomacy metadata scaffolding

The diplomacy entries are not applied to Freeciv diplomatic state yet. They are
metadata for future scenario enrichment because the current safe server/Lua
authoring path does not expose arbitrary initial diplomacy editing.

Historical regions are defined in:

- `data/organic_history/scenario_regions.json` for Python tooling
- `data/organic_history/scenario_regions.lua` for Lua-facing conventions

The current region boxes are for the 80x50 earth-small coordinate space:
Americas, Europe, Near East, Africa, Steppe, India, and China.

Run a scenario directly:

```sh
python3 tools/organic_history/run_ai_game.py \
  --ruleset-serv data/organic_history.serv \
  --load-scenario data/organic_history/scenarios/earth_ancient_v0.sav \
  --turns 20 \
  --players 8 \
  --output-dir runs/organic_history_scenario_load_test \
  --clean-output-dir \
  --timeout 240
```

Regenerate all v0 fixtures plus the authored ancient v1 fixture:

```sh
python3 tools/organic_history/create_scenario_fixture.py --include-v1
```

Validate v1 and its expected players, cities, gold, technologies, and research:

```sh
python3 tools/organic_history/validate_scenario.py \
  data/organic_history/scenarios/earth_ancient_v1.sav \
  --starts-plan data/organic_history/scenarios/earth_ancient_v1_starts.json \
  --turns 20 \
  --players 7 \
  --output-dir runs/organic_history_ancient_v1_validate \
  --timeout 240
```

Run the fast scenario gate:

```sh
tools/organic_history/scenario_gate.sh
```
